{"reference":"Isaiah 25","book":"Isaiah","chapter":25,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Death Defeated","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One debated reading sees Isaiah 25:6-9 as part of a wider pattern in Isaiah 25-27 and 65-66: death’s defeat appears alongside bodily revival, transformed longevity, renewed Jerusalem, and new-heavens-and-earth imagery. This pattern became foundational for later Jewish and Christian hope concerning resurrection and new creation.","verse_refs":["Isaiah 25:6-9"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_025_ba0f72b86e27371f2346ef6f"]},{"id":"block_2","text":"A debated later reception of verse 8 connects its declaration that death is swallowed up with Paul’s use of death-defeat and death-taunt language, thanksgiving, and a call to steadfast labor. The connection places hope in the face of death alongside ongoing work rather than treating them as opposites.","verse_refs":["Isaiah 25:8"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_025_e42932f47dbd347f50ad27b2"]}]},{"kind":"why_it_matters","title":"Hope, Grief, and Vocation","blocks":[{"id":"block_3","text":"This later use matters because it holds hope, grief, and vocation together: steadfastness is not presented as compulsory overwork or as a denial of loss.","verse_refs":["Isaiah 25:8"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_025_34fc4adce3c087378a93a290"]}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"A Manuscript Witness to Isaiah","blocks":[{"id":"block_4","text":"One disputed scholarly description notes that the Great Isaiah Scroll preserves an almost complete witness to all sixty-six chapters of Isaiah. It broadly aligns with the Masoretic tradition while also containing thousands of spelling and substantive differences; other Isaiah manuscripts and interpretive writings from Qumran likewise show active transmission and interpretation of the book.","confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_025_424fae724100aed0421eccbf"]}]}],"generated_metadata":null}